infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Three cache invalidations after a mutation — pick by trust in the response
  desc All three refresh stale queries; they differ in network cost and what they assume the mutation response contains
  lists
    - label setQueryData — write the response straight into cache
      desc Cheapest: no extra network call. Correct only when the mutation response carries the complete new entity state. Use it for the directly-mutated entity.
    - label invalidateQueries — mark stale, refetch on next observer
      desc Safest: guaranteed canonical server data, at the cost of one background refetch. Use it for listing queries that still reference the old entity.
    - label refetchQueries — force an immediate fetch now
      desc Most eager: fetch right away when you need fresh data and cannot trust the mutation response. Most network, least patient.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
